    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.statusline\n\n### Description\n\nt would be great to have the ability to customize the highlights for each diagnostic level (e.g., Error, Warn, Info, Hint) in the mini.statusline plugin. This enhancement would allow users to visually distinguish between different types of diagnostics more easily in the statusline.",
