            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThis is already possible via utilizing [`signs` option of `section_diagnostics()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/df1559e2ed7ece458e0a97a8bb9556d465d1c775/doc/mini-statusline.txt#L271-L274). Because the output of any `config.content` method is treated as a regular string for statusline (see `:h statusline`), signs can also use special characters to change their highlighting (`%#HighlightGroupName#` in particular).\r\n\r\nHere is an example of how to achieve this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal diag_signs = {\r\n  ERROR = '%#DiagnosticError#E',\r\n  WARN  = '%#DiagnosticWarn#W',\r\n  INFO  = '%#DiagnosticInfo#I',\r\n  HINT  = '%#DiagnosticHint#H',\r\n}\r\n\r\nlocal active_content = function()\r\n  local mode, mode_hl = MiniStatusline.section_mode({ trunc_width = 120 })\r\n  local git           = MiniStatusline.section_git({ trunc_width = 40 })\r\n  local diff          = MiniStatusline.section_diff({ trunc_width = 75 })\r\n  local lsp           = MiniStatusline.section_lsp({ trunc_width = 75 })\r\n  local filename      = MiniStatusline.section_filename({ trunc_width = 140 })\r\n  local fileinfo      = MiniStatusline.section_fileinfo({ trunc_width = 120 })\r\n  local location      = MiniStatusline.section_location({ trunc_width = 75 })\r\n  local search        = MiniStatusline.section_searchcount({ trunc_width = 75 })\r\n\r\n  -- Compute colored diagnostics and reset color for later LSP section\r\n  local diagnostics = MiniStatusline.section_diagnostics({ trunc_width = 75, signs = diag_signs })\r\n  diagnostics = diagnostics .. '%#MiniStatuslineDevinfo#'\r\n\r\n  return MiniStatusline.combine_groups({\r\n    { hl = mode_hl,                  strings = { mode } },\r\n    { hl = 'MiniStatuslineDevinfo',  strings = { git, diff, diagnostics, lsp } },\r\n    '%<', -- Mark general truncate point\r\n    { hl = 'MiniStatuslineFilename', strings = { filename } },\r\n    '%=', -- End left alignment\r\n    { hl = 'MiniStatuslineFileinfo', strings = { fileinfo } },\r\n    { hl = mode_hl,                  strings = { search, location } },\r\n  })\r\nend\r\n\r\nrequire('mini.statusline').setup({ content = { active = active_content } })\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf run this setup, you'd probably notice that highlighted diagnostics have \"good colored\" foreground (text color) but not matching background color. This is an issue with how statusline computes its colors (it doesn't properly \"combine\" colors)  and is one of the main reasons why 'mini.statusline' and 'mini.tabline' don't come with built-in color support. There are attempts to make it work in Neovim, but (as far as my initial tests show) they are not ideal yet.\r\n\r\nThe solution to this highlighting problem is to define your own highlight groups (something like `Diagnost{Error,Warn,Info,Hint}Statusline`) which will have both foreground and background.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nClosing as already possible (albeit with extra hurdles).",
